{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And He said, My Presence shall go, etc.</b> Many interpretations have been offered on these verses. It appears proper to explain the verse according to the words of the holy ones of blessed memory (Tikkunim 18) that His Shekhinah, may He be blessed, is called ״פְּנֵי ה׳״ [the Face of YHWH] because it is that which is seen by the host of heaven, and to it alludes His saying (Exodus 23:15): ״וְלֹא יֵרָאוּ פָנַי רֵיקָם״. And here YHWH answered Moses regarding his claims and informed him that the one going with him is <b>the Face of YHWH</b>, which is the Shekhinah; and concerning the concern that perhaps this presence would not be restful for Moses, He said <b>and I will give you rest</b>." "<b>And it further intends</b> to tell him that a supernal light would rest upon him and not depart from him — that which had rested upon him until now from the spirit — but that for the aspect of Israel the Shekhinah would go before them, and this aspect is an aspect of judgment, and the Name that declares of it is Adonai; and concerning this Moses answered and said <b>If Your Presence does not go</b>, etc. (Exodus 33:15):"], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:26.576681110Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}